+// ── bad-scan rejection (divergence hardening) ──────────────────────────────────
+// A physically-impossible LiDAR correction (a fridge door / arm sweeping the near FOV during
+// manipulation) is ROLLED BACK instead of applied, and its scan is NOT inserted into the map, so a
+// transient bad scan cannot corrupt the estimator and diverge the odom. The pre-update (IMU-
+// predicted) state already contains this interval's real motion, so a large pre->post correction
+// means the LiDAR measurement disagrees with the IMU — the divergence signature. Sustained rejects
+// are counted + warned; the 360 deg MID360 keeps good static geometry (sides/rear) during a
+// front-FOV disturbance, so short disturbances ride through on IMU + the static majority.
+bool   reject_enable       = true;
